@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Historical / alternative. Dated observation or rejected/unselected alternative is preserved without becoming a current MVP topology.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #486777
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #EEF5FA
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #486777
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F7FAFC
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3DA
skinparam noteBorderColor #B59865
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
title HISTORICAL / UNSELECTED — Infrastructure topology — observed demo and explicit gaps
top to bottom direction
node "Browser client" as browser
node "Authorized operator workstation" as operator
node "Hetzner VM\nUbuntu 24.04.4 LTS\n2 vCPU / 4 GB allocated / 40 GB local disk" as host {
 artifact "Nginx active\nPublic /login responded" as web
 artifact "PHP 8.3-FPM active\nLaravel application files / lockfile" as app
 database "MySQL 8.0.46 active\nApplication connection not inspected" as db
}
browser --> web : HTTPS observed in dated record
operator --> host : SSH used for historical read-only inspection
rectangle "Recovery capability gap\nOwner reports backups not configured\nNo independent protected backup proven" as backup #FFF3DA
rectangle "Availability capability gap\nNo standby, replication or failover evidence\nNo selected HA / DR topology" as ha #FFF3DA
host ..> backup : evidence needed; not an existing link
host ..> ha : single observed host; no redundancy claimed
note bottom of ha
Service presence does not prove application-to-database connectivity.
Firewall rules, private network zones and backend transport were not inspected.
No load balancer, secondary host or paid service is assumed.
end note

legend bottom
Historical inventory: November 1, 2026, not a current live inspection or selected final architecture.
Solid arrows: recorded access paths. Dashed arrows: identified capability gaps, not configured connections.
endlegend
@enduml
